{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>לכן.</b> Because he did a fitting thing before HaShem — 'therefore I give him My covenant of peace.' And if Israel hate him, he will not worry, and he need not fear — neither the relatives of Zimri nor the relatives of Cozbi, for she was a king's daughter. And in Kiddushin, chapter האומר, it concludes: the vav of שלום is cut off — for midrash, when it is whole [shalem] and not when it is defective. From here: a priest with a blemish, whose service is invalid."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:12.381469324Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}